  "body": "Found by the other session's safety review of #1397 (2026-11-13). On main, the Fanuc Lathe live-tool path (`liveMove`, via #1395's lathe rotary-cap call) measures a move on the UNROUNDED r/z/C, but the post writes rounded words. #1395 fixed this posted-coordinate rule for fanuc and doosan mills; the lathe call is only half-applied. A probe drives X/Z about **7.4% over fmax** when judged from the posted words.\n\n**Done means:** the lathe live-tool feed cap measures the move on the posted (rounded, origin-relative) X/Z/C words, the same as #1395 does for the mills, so neither the rotary rate nor fmax is exceeded by the posted program. Pin it with the review's probe case, mutation-checked. Coordinate with #1397, which touches the same code.\n",
